Regression test for the textarea value-update path. `textarea(:value=v)` and
`input(:value=v)` must SetText the value at BuildUI time and re-sync the entry
whenever the var changes. A one-way `value=expr` is only where the widget's own
cell starts (testdata/unbound_prop_state.txtar), so the fixture binds.

Reactivity flows through the shared NoReactivity lowering pass, which splices
an explicit `m.__n0.SetText(...)` after every Assign that mutates a tracked
var, rather than emitting a per-widget updateEntry0 method. That spliced
re-sync is spelled identically to the BuildUI-time call, so only the pair --
the assignment in the @click handler followed by the SetText -- tells the two
claims apart. SetText takes the value unwrapped: the Entry intrinsic declares
`text string`, so the caller converts and no fmt.Sprint appears around it.
Widget ids are the lowered __nN scheme: textarea __n0, vbox __n1, button __n2.

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go { fyne(main=true) }
}

window #app(title="t") {
    var content = "initial value"

    vbox {
        textarea(:value=content, rows=4)
        button(text="set", @click { content = "after click" })
    }
}
